  "description": "In this report, we analyze the compromise of Reactor, starting with the identification of Next.js 15.0.3 on port 3000. Exploitation of CVE-2025-55182 (React Server Components RCE) provided initial access as the node user. Local enumeration revealed an SQLite database containing password hashes, which were cracked offline to gain SSH access as the engineer user. Finally, privilege escalation was achieved by abusing an unauthenticated Node.js Inspector interface running as root on port 9229 to execute arbitrary commands.",
